 "verdict": "ONE LAW, TWO WINDOWS: X182 controlled the pattern value at the pair's midpoint and X184 controlled the local inflow at the colder body, with opposite signs in the manipulated variable and both pre-registered. Read on the single axis the second experiment identified, the colder body's inflow, the two experiments land on the same curve: F_local 0.000-0.019 gives 0 of 22 = 0.00; F_local 0.019-0.024 gives 5 of 11 = 0.45; F_local 0.028-0.032 gives 15 of 15 = 1.00; F_local 0.032-0.040 gives 10 of 10 = 1.00. The design's own reason is geometric: the bodies are 16 cells apart, 120 degrees of the pattern's 12-cell period, so a cold midpoint implies warm bodies - which is why X182's bottom level (midpoint G 0.067) fused 1.00 while its top level (midpoint G 0.933) fused 0.00. Line by line the two windows agree, and the bands that are too thin (0.024-0.028) carry no weight."
